  <data key="d7">CH02_EN_PDF001_B002</data>
</edge>
<edge source="MATH6_C0019" target="MATH6_C0020">
  <data key="d4">0.96</data>
  <data key="d5">An angle is defined as the figure formed by two rays sharing a common starting point; therefore understanding rays precedes learning about angles.</data>
  <data key="d6">PENDING</data>
  <data key="d7">CH02_EN_PDF005_B004</data>
</edge>
<edge source="MATH6_C0019" target="MATH6_C0021">
  <data key="d4">0.94</data>
  <data key="d5">The concept of a vertex is introduced as the common starting point of two rays in the definition of an angle, so knowledge of rays is required before learning what a vertex is.</data>
