<edge source="MATH6_C0019" target="MATH6_C0023">
  <data key="d4">0.9</data>
  <data key="d5">A straight angle is described as a 180° turn formed by two opposite rays; knowledge of rays is required to grasp this concept.</data>
  <data key="d6">PENDING</data>
  <data key="d7">CH02_EN_PDF003_B001;CH02_EN_PDF015_B004</data>
</edge>
<edge source="MATH6_C0019" target="MATH6_C0024">
  <data key="d4">0.9</data>
  <data key="d5">A right angle is defined as a 90° turn between two rays; understanding rays precedes learning right angles.</data>
