</edge>
<edge source="MATH6_C0019" target="MATH6_C0031">
  <data key="d4">0.65</data>
  <data key="d5">Perpendicular lines are described as two lines meeting at a right angle. A right angle is an angle formed by two rays, so grasping the concept of a ray supports understanding perpendicularity.</data>
